-- Heroic dungeon rows that keep the normal-mode level although ref_cpp has a heroic template 25 levels higher: set level (and, for elites, DamageModifier) from the ref_cpp heroic template.
-- Cause: 25 DUNGEON_HEROIC rows (Utgarde Keep, The Nexus, Halls of Stone, Azjol-Nerub, Ahn'kahet, Violet Hold, Blackrock Caverns, Lordaeron specimens ...) have level 65-79 while the
--   ref_cpp heroic template (difficulty_entry_1 of the normal entry) is level 70-86 (3-10 levels higher, 80-81 for the WotLK dungeons). The DamageModifier set by heroic-dm (files 10/11)
--   was computed on the old (too low) level, so it is recomputed here with the same formula on the ref_cpp heroic level.
-- Rules: rank 0 = level only (DamageModifier unchanged); rank >= 1 = heroic-dm rules A1 (exp 0-2) / A3 (exp 3) at the new level. Must be applied after 2026_11_03_10/_11.
-- Source: ref_cpp creature_template (difficulty_entry_1 -> heroic template level/health/DM) and creature_classlevelstats, our creature_classlevelstats, heroic-dm rules (commits 86c9ad52, 63f924a9).
-- Rollback: every UPDATE carries the old values (state after files 10/11) in its trailing comment; full script state/hdm/heroic_dm_rollback_14.sql

UPDATE `creature_template_difficulty` SET `level_min` = 71, `level_max` = 71, `DamageModifier` = 1.0 WHERE `id` = 17399 AND `difficulty` = 'DUNGEON_HEROIC'; -- Seductress rk 0 exp 1 no spawn, old L61-61 DM 1.0, cpp heroic template 18614 (L71-71 hm 1.35 dm 5.9)
